From e5d3f4474060af864550c7568bff34bc2c1acc46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leon_fang <leon_fang@realsil.com.cn>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 10:45:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Add zero-copy streaming extraction for firmware upload

Implement streaming tar extraction during HTTP reception to eliminate
memory buffering. Data flows directly from HTTP socket to tar extraction
pipe, reducing memory usage for updating firmware images. For now, it
only supports '/redfish/v1/UpdateService/update' http push method

BMCSW-775

Change-Id: I908f59949e4822ce66a5079fee815552fc02b148
Signed-off-by: leon_fang <leon_fang@realsil.com.cn>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local configuration change for realtek, not suitable for upstream]
